            1. The Short Answer: Which Under Sink Filter to Buy
          </h2>

          <p>
            An under sink water filter is the best balance of cost, capacity and filtration for drinking and cooking water. A pitcher holds a few cups and needs refilling all day; a whole-house system treats the water you flush and wash the car with, which you do not need to drink. An under sink system sits in the cabinet, treats only the water that comes out of one faucet, and does it at a cost per gallon that is far lower than a pitcher.
          </p>

          <p>
            The problem is that the category is crowded with near-identical listings that make the same claims: 99% of lead, PFAS, heavy metals, microplastics. Those claims are often not backed by any certification at all. The quickest way through the noise is to ignore the box and look for the NSF/ANSI standard numbers, and the name of the body that tested the product. That is how this list is ranked.
          </p>

          <p>
            If you want one answer, buy the <strong>Aquasana Claryum 3-Stage</strong>. It is certified to NSF/ANSI 42, 53 and 401, which covers chlorine taste, lead, PFOA/PFOS and a long list of other contaminants. If you want the same certification for less money, buy the <strong>A.O. Smith AO-US-200</strong>. If your water is already safe and simply tastes of chlorine, the <strong>Waterdrop 10UA</strong> is cheap to buy and cheap to run. If your water report shows high dissolved solids, nitrates or arsenic, carbon will not help and you need reverse osmosis: the <strong>iSpring RCC7AK</strong> with a tank, or the <strong>Waterdrop G3P800</strong> without one.
          </p>

          <p>
            Before you buy any of them, find your utility's annual water quality report, often called a Consumer Confidence Report, or test a well. The report tells you whether you are solving a taste problem or a health problem, and that one fact decides most of this page. If you are still deciding between an under sink unit and treating the whole house, start with our <a href="/best-water-filtration-system-for-home/">guide to the best water filtration systems for home</a>, which compares every type side by side.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8 my-8">
